HKUDS/ViMax
https://github.com/HKUDS/ViMax (commit 01b4696ebb54805dc465f5f815f5ee87891909d8)

What was taken: the storyboard rules and the shot decomposition of agents/storyboard_artist.py
(system_prompt_template_design_storyboard, system_prompt_template_decompose_visual_description, and the
first-frame / last-frame / motion / variation_type fields of VisDescDecompositionResponse and interfaces/shot_description.py),
adapted into prompt text and TypeScript types.

Where: command-center/lib/brain/prompt.ts (PLAN_SYSTEM_PROMPT, "How you shoot"), command-center/lib/brain/logic.ts (the shot
spec types), command-center/lib/brain/plan.ts (the checks of those rules).

Also taken (character reference sheets): the three portrait prompts of agents/character_portraits_generator.py
(prompt_template_front, prompt_template_side, prompt_template_back) and its order (the front from words, the side and the back
from the front); the reference rules of agents/reference_image_selector.py (at most 8 pictures, at most one view per character,
the view the shot shows, "Image N" counted from 0 by position in the selected list), re-written as deterministic code rather than
a language-model call; and the per-scene character with its own features of interfaces/character.py (CharacterInScene).

Where: command-center/lib/brain/ref-sheets.ts (sheetPrompt, planSheets, selectRefs, wantedView).

